# Trivy ignore file (auto-read by the fs scan in .github/workflows/trivy.yml).
# Each entry is an accepted-risk finding that can't be fixed cleanly right now.
# Keep a justification + tracking issue + revisit date with every entry.
# NOTE: plain .trivyignore matches IDs repo-wide (no per-path scoping), so any
# NEW Dockerfile must still add a non-root USER — DS-0002 is suppressed below.

# AVD-DS-0002 (HIGH) — "Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with a
# non-root user." Triggered only by client/Dockerfile, whose final nginx:alpine
# stage runs as root (stock nginx needs root to bind :80). client/Dockerfile is
# a DEV-ONLY artifact — PW v2 deploys from pw.json + the platform service
# catalog's nginx image, not this file. A proper fix (nginx-unprivileged on
# :8080) ripples into nginx.conf / compose port mapping; tracked in #46.
# (server/Dockerfile already runs as USER node and is unaffected.)
# Revisit by: 2026-09-01
AVD-DS-0002
